Add the Helm repository: 
------------------------
>> helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts

>> helm repo udpate

Look the helm repo for the charts
-----------------------------------------
>> helm search repo prometheus-community

Find the available chart version: 
-----------------------------------------
>> helm search repo prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack

Create the monitoring namespace
-----------------------------------------
>> kubectl create namespace monitoring

Check the chart configuration before installation
---------------------------------------------------
>> helm show values prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack > /tmp/kube-prometheus-default-values.yaml


And create a custom configuration file to provide our value
-----------------------------------------------------------

>> touch values.yaml

Here we will configure the following things: 

Prometheus Operator: Enabled
Prometheus         : Enabled , persistent storage ,15-day retention
Grafana            : Enabled , persistent storage, dashboard provisioning
AlertManager       : Enabled , persistent storage
Node Exporter      : Enabled
Kube-state-metrics : Enabled
ServiceMonitor discovery : Enabled for monitoring additional namespace
Istio metrics            : Integrated after the initial stack is healthy


Next Check your Storage Class: 
--------------------------------

>> kubectl get storageclass

Check the monitoring namespace:
--------------------------------
>> kubectl get namespace monitoring



Install the monitoring Stack : 

>> 

helm upgrade --install prometheus-stack \
  prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
  --version 92.16.0 \
  --namespace monitoring \
  --create-namespace \
  -f values.yaml \
  --wait \
  --timeout 10m

Check wheather the resources are installed or not:
>> kubectl get pod -n monitoring

AFTER 

Step 1: Check the Prometheus targets : 

>>
 kubectl port-forward -n monitoring svc/prometheus-stack-kube-prom-prometheus 9090:9090


